Ploy search attribution
=======================

The two-player lookahead is a Rust/WebAssembly adaptation of the search
architecture documented in Dr. Thomas Tensi's open-source Ada Ploy engine:
iterative deepening, MTD(f), alpha-beta, Zobrist fingerprints, a transposition
table, make/unmake, refutation/history ordering, bounded recapture and
Commander-threat extensions, and bounded capture quiescence. It is adapted
for bounded WASM memory and deterministic node budgets.

Upstream project and source:
https://tensi.eu/thomas/programming/games/ploy/ploy.html

Copyright (c) 2013, Dr. Thomas Tensi

The upstream MIT license is reproduced in TENSI-LICENSE.

Only the search architecture is adapted. This remaster's rules follow the
1970 3M instruction sheet; the later rule variants in the Ada program are not
used.
